<main class="tm">
  <h1>Founding Circle Challenge: full terms</h1>
  <p class="tm-lead">The short version: share your code with friends who would value DhiRise. When a friend finishes the full check and gives honest feedback, it counts. The person with the most valid referrals wins.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>1. Who runs it</h2>
    <p>The DhiRise Founding Circle Challenge ("the challenge") is run by DhiRise. By joining, you agree to these terms.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. Dates</h2>
    <p>The challenge is open now and ends on <b>30 October 2026 at 11:59 pm IST</b>. Referrals completed after that time do not count.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. Who can take part</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Students from Class 8 up to college, living in India.</li>
      <li>If you are under 18, a parent or guardian must agree before you join. We may ask them to confirm.</li>
      <li>One account per person. DhiRise team members and their families can't win.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. The prize</h2>
    <p>The top referrer wins <b>one gift hamper worth ₹2,999</b>, which may include shoes, headphones and apparel. Items depend on availability and sizes, and may be swapped for items of similar value. The prize can't be exchanged for cash.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. What counts as a valid referral</h2>
    <p>A referral counts only when your friend:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>signs in with a new email that has never used DhiRise before,</li>
      <li>enters your code when signing in (or opens your link),</li>
      <li>finishes all 18 questions,</li>
      <li>reaches their report, and</li>
      <li>submits genuine feedback in their own words.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can't refer yourself, use extra accounts, or ask people to give fake answers or feedback. Referrals that don't meet every step show as "pending" and do not count.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Ranking and review</h2>
    <p>The leaderboard ranks people by valid referrals. If two people have the same number, the one who reached it first ranks higher. The leaderboard updates every few minutes and may change during review.</p>
    <p>After the challenge ends, we review the top 10 by hand. We may remove referrals that look fake or break these rules. The person with the most valid referrals after review wins. DhiRise's decision is final.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. How the winner is contacted</h2>
    <p>We announce the winner on the leaderboard and contact them at the email they signed in with, and on the mobile number they gave us, if any. For a winner under 18, we also contact their parent or guardian. If we can't reach the winner within 7 days, or they don't meet these terms, the prize goes to the next person after review.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>8. Your data</h2>
    <p>We use your name, class, referral code and referral count to run the challenge and show the leaderboard. The leaderboard only shows your first name, the first letter of your surname, your class and your style. We don't sell your data. Your check answers are used as described when you signed in.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>9. Changes</h2>
    <p>If something outside our control affects the challenge, we may change or end it early and will say so on this page.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions, or want your data removed? Write to <a href="mailto:privacy@dhirise.com">privacy@dhirise.com</a>.</p>
  </section>
</main>
